{
  "description": "",
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "What this shows:\nRetrieval change compared with normal behavior.\n\nWhy you care:\nRAG quality can change when context selection changes.\n\nHow to read it:\nRising retrieval change means retrieved context differs from normal.\n\nWhat to do next:\nInspect query groups and index or corpus updates.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 16,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "mcRecipe": {
        "expectedMetrics": [
          "metricchrono_ai_retrieval_change_score"
        ],
        "tableColumns": [],
        "unitMarking": "percent"
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(metricchrono_ai_retrieval_change_score{service=\"$service\",environment=\"$environment\",model=\"$model\",comparison=\"normal_baseline\"})",
          "format": "time_series",
          "legendFormat": "retrieval changed compared to normal",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Is retrieval behavior changing?",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "What this shows:\nRetrieval change beside output change.\n\nWhy you care:\nChanged context can lead to changed answers.\n\nHow to read it:\nIf both lines rise together, retrieval may be driving output movement.\n\nWhat to do next:\nInspect retrieved context examples.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 16,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 2,
      "mcRecipe": {
        "expectedMetrics": [
          "metricchrono_ai_output_change_score",
          "metricchrono_ai_retrieval_change_score"
        ],
        "tableColumns": [],
        "unitMarking": "percent"
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(metricchrono_ai_retrieval_change_score{service=\"$service\",environment=\"$environment\",model=\"$model\"})",
          "format": "time_series",
          "legendFormat": "Retrieval",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(metricchrono_ai_output_change_score{service=\"$service\",environment=\"$environment\",model=\"$model\"})",
          "format": "time_series",
          "legendFormat": "Outputs",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Are retrieval changes affecting output behavior?",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "What this shows:\nRetrieval movement beside model-version state.\n\nWhy you care:\nRollouts and index updates often explain retrieval shifts.\n\nHow to read it:\nA jump after v2 becomes active is deploy-correlated.\n\nWhat to do next:\nCheck deploy or index update notes.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 16,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "id": 3,
      "mcRecipe": {
        "expectedMetrics": [
          "metricchrono_ai_model_version_active",
          "metricchrono_ai_retrieval_change_score"
        ],
        "tableColumns": [],
        "unitMarking": "none"
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max by (model_version) (metricchrono_ai_model_version_active{service=\"$service\",environment=\"$environment\",model=\"$model\"})",
          "format": "time_series",
          "legendFormat": "{{model_version}} active",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(metricchrono_ai_retrieval_change_score{service=\"$service\",environment=\"$environment\",model=\"$model\"})",
          "format": "time_series",
          "legendFormat": "Retrieval change",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Did retrieval change after a deploy or index update?",
      "type": "state-timeline"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "What this shows:\nRetrieval-related rows ranked by change.\n\nWhy you care:\nThis gives a concrete place to inspect.\n\nHow to read it:\nStart with the highest score.\n\nWhat to do next:\nInspect example queries from that stream.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 16,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8
      },
      "id": 4,
      "mcRecipe": {
        "expectedMetrics": [
          "metricchrono_ai_inspection_candidate"
        ],
        "tableColumns": [
          "stream",
          "workload",
          "model_version",
          "change_score",
          "next_step"
        ],
        "unitMarking": "percent"
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "topk(6, max by (stream,workload,model_version,main_change,cause,next_step,drift_state) (max_over_time(metricchrono_ai_inspection_candidate{service=\"$service\",environment=\"$environment\",model=\"$model\",workload=\"retrieval\"}[$__range])))",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "retrieval candidate",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Which query group changed most?",
      "type": "table"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "What this shows:\nRetrieval movement compared with last window and normal behavior.\n\nWhy you care:\nSudden shifts suggest deploy or index incidents; gradual shifts suggest corpus or query drift.\n\nHow to read it:\nSudden change spikes; drift from normal accumulates.\n\nWhat to do next:\nPick deploy or data investigation based on the shape.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 16,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "id": 5,
      "mcRecipe": {
        "expectedMetrics": [
          "metricchrono_ai_retrieval_change_score"
        ],
        "tableColumns": [],
        "unitMarking": "percent"
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(metricchrono_ai_retrieval_change_score{service=\"$service\",environment=\"$environment\",model=\"$model\",comparison=\"last_window\"})",
          "format": "time_series",
          "legendFormat": "Sudden retrieval change",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(metricchrono_ai_retrieval_change_score{service=\"$service\",environment=\"$environment\",model=\"$model\",comparison=\"normal_baseline\"})",
          "format": "time_series",
          "legendFormat": "Retrieval drift from normal",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Is this sudden or gradual retrieval drift?",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "What this shows:\nCurrent retrieval behavior state.\n\nWhy you care:\nRAG users need a simple status before drilling into documents.\n\nHow to read it:\n0 is Normal, 1 is Watch, 2 is Drift, and 3 is Incident.\n\nWhat to do next:\nIf this is elevated, inspect retrieval candidates.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 16,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16
      },
      "id": 6,
      "mcRecipe": {
        "expectedMetrics": [
          "metricchrono_ai_drift_state"
        ],
        "tableColumns": [],
        "unitMarking": "none"
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(metricchrono_ai_drift_state{service=\"$service\",environment=\"$environment\",model=\"$model\",workload=\"retrieval\"})",
          "format": "time_series",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "RAG status",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Current RAG status?",
      "type": "stat"
    }
  ],
  "refresh": "5s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "tags": [
    "ai-observability",
    "mlops",
    "metricchrono",
    "recipe"
  ],
